@startuml
!include ../shortfall/style.iuml
title Setting targets: parse, then update the saved targets
autonumber

actor "User" as User
participant "mishMash:MishMash" as App
participant "parser:Parser" as Parser
participant "setTargetsParser:SetTargetsParser" as SParser
participant "changes:TargetChanges" as Changes
participant "set:SetTargetsCommand" as Set
participant "settings:TargetSettings" as Settings

User -> App : set-targets cal/2000 p/none
App -> Parser : parseCommand(input)
activate Parser
create SParser
Parser -> SParser : new SetTargetsParser()
activate SParser
SParser --> Parser : setTargetsParser
deactivate SParser
Parser -> SParser : parse("cal/2000 p/none")
activate SParser
alt blank, unknown or repeated prefix, or invalid value
  SParser --> Parser : throws IllegalArgumentException
  deactivate SParser
  Parser --> App : throws MishMashException (message ends with the set-targets format)
  deactivate Parser
  App -> User : display the error
  note over App, Settings : Parsing stops before any command exists, so the saved targets are unchanged.
else every token is valid
  create Changes
  SParser -> Changes : new TargetChanges(cal=Optional.of(2000), p=Optional.empty())
  activate Changes
  Changes --> SParser : changes
  deactivate Changes
  SParser --> Parser : changes
  deactivate SParser
  create Set
  Parser -> Set : new SetTargetsCommand(changes, settings)
  activate Set
  Set --> Parser : command
  deactivate Set
  Parser --> App : command
  deactivate Parser
  App -> Set : execute(recipeBook)
  activate Set
  Set -> Settings : get()
  Settings --> Set : current targets
  Set -> Changes : applyTo(current)
  Changes --> Set : updated targets (calories replaced, protein removed, others kept)
  Set -> Settings : set(updated)
  Set --> App : confirmation and current-plan reminder
  deactivate Set
  App -> User : display the result
end

note over Parser, Settings
  Dispatch on the command word and logging are condensed. The recipe book passed to execute
  is not used, and ActiveMealPlan is not involved, so an existing plan keeps its own targets.
end note
@enduml
